# Code review and validation

Use this checklist on AI-generated or human diffs. Passing the checklist is not a production guarantee.

## Architecture

- [ ] Type lives in the existing `com.automation.*` package for that job
- [ ] No new Maven dependency, package, or GitHub Actions edit unless requested
- [ ] No PageFactory, Extent, Excel, SLF4J, or `Thread.sleep`
- [ ] Driver only via `DriverFactory`; tests extend `BaseTest`

## Pages

- [ ] `private static final By` locators; `id` / `data-test` preferred
- [ ] Actions use `click` / `type` / `getText` / `isDisplayed` / `findVisible`
- [ ] Fluent return: `this` or next page; `isLoaded()` present
- [ ] No TestNG asserts in pages
- [ ] Success navigation waits via `WaitUtils.waitForUrlContains` where existing pages do

## Tests

- [ ] `should*` name, `groups`, `description`
- [ ] Independent (self-login); uses `LoginDataProvider` constants
- [ ] Class listed in both TestNG XMLs if it is a new class
- [ ] Assertions have messages; locators not in business tests

## Config / waits

- [ ] `implicitWait` still 0; no hardcoded 30s waits
- [ ] New config keys added to `config.properties` **and** a `ConfigReader` accessor if introduced

## Validate (run what you can)

```text
mvn -q -DskipTests compile test-compile
mvn test -Dtest=TheChangedTestClass
# or
mvn test -Psmoke "-Dheadless=true"
```

Report exactly: compile result, which tests ran, which were skipped, screenshots/Allure if a failure was investigated.

## Contradiction watch

- Do not “fix” JS click by adding native click in one page while `BasePage.click` remains JS-based — change is global.
- Do not add `@Step` on `src/main/java` (Allure is test-scoped).
- Do not raise `RetryAnalyzer.MAX_RETRY` to green a flake.
- Do not treat `FrameworkSmokeTest` locators as a template for `LoginTests`.
